  "notes": "Built from the archived 2024-25 bulletin (fetched raw HTML directly, cross-checked against its own printed Suggested Academic Plan subtotals, which sum to its own stated 'Total Credits 120'). Requirements for the Major section (Prescribed Courses GLIS 101N/102N/400Y, 6cr beyond-level-12/second-world-language requirement, 21cr Pathway courses with 15cr in one concentration + 6cr from others + 12cr at 400-level-or-higher) is confirmed byte-identical to the 2026 edition -- no real major-requirement change. Uses the same reformed post-Fall-2023 General Education model as the 2026 file (Foundations GQ 6cr/GWS 9cr, Knowledge Domains 3cr each, 6cr Inter-Domain, 9cr Exploration) -- confirmed unchanged from the 2023-24 edition by direct diff. 2024-25 is the first archived edition to switch to 'World Language'/'second world language' and 'World Cultures' terminology (2022-23 and 2023-24 both still say 'Foreign Language'/'Other Cultures' -- see GLISBA-2022.json / GLISBA-2023.json), so this file already matches the 2026 file's wording exactly; no relabeling needed. The 2024-25 Suggested Academic Plan is still a single combined 'University Park Campus and Commonwealth Campuses' 8-semester table (120 total credits, no LA 83/LA 283 items) -- confirmed by direct diff against the 2025-26 archive that the UP/Commonwealth split with LA 83/LA 283 (1.5cr advising-seminar items each) and the jump to 123cr (UP) first appears starting the 2025-26 edition, one year after this one; so this plan (like the 2026 file, which also omits LA 83/LA 283 entirely) needs no such items. Global Conflict Pathway substitute courses (PLSC 14, GEOG 126, HIST 120/420, PLSC 414, PLSC 458, PLSC 437, CMLIT 449, COMM 410) are not named in the bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan (only generic 'Major Course from List' / '4XX Level Major Course' placeholders are printed there, since the real departmental Pathway list is not published in the bulletin) -- carried over from the 2026 file's own curatorial pick after directly confirming each exact course code existed in the 2024-25 university-course-descriptions catalog (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/university-course-descriptions/undergraduate/{geog,cmlit}/ spot-checked; all five departments already confirmed present in the bracketing 2022-23 catalog), not assumed.",
